.TH GIT-WTMIGRATE 1 2026-10-21 dotfiles "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-wtmigrate \- convert an existing clone into the bare worktree layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git wtmigrate
.RI [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts a regular clone into the layout that
.BR git\-wtclone (1)
creates. For a clone at
.I foo
whose main checkout is on branch
.IR main :
.PP
.RS
.nf
before                      after
foo/                        foo/.git       (bare repository)
foo/.git/                   foo/main/      (former main checkout)
foo-feature-x/  (worktree)  foo/feature-x/ (moved worktree)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Every file in the main checkout stays as it was, including uncommitted,
staged, untracked, and ignored files. The former
.I .git
folder becomes the bare repository in place, so worktrees that are not
moved keep working.
.PP
Linked worktrees that are on a branch move to
.IR foo/<branch> .
Detached or locked worktrees, and worktrees whose target folder already
exists, stay where they are, with a warning.
.PP
Shells that were inside the old main checkout keep a stale path; run
.B cd
to the new folder afterwards.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I path
Any folder inside the repository to convert, including a linked worktree.
Defaults to the current folder.
.SH REFUSED CASES
.B git wtmigrate
stops without changing anything when:
.IP \(bu 2
the repository already uses the bare layout;
.IP \(bu 2
the main checkout has a detached HEAD;
.IP \(bu 2
a merge, rebase, cherry-pick, revert, or bisect is in progress;
.IP \(bu 2
the repository has initialized submodules;
.IP \(bu 2
.I core.worktree
is set;
.IP \(bu 2
a linked worktree sits inside the main checkout;
.IP \(bu 2
two worktrees would get the same folder name.
.SH FAILURE
The checkout is first moved to a temporary folder named
.I .<repo>.wtmigrate.XXXXXX
next to the repository. If a step fails after that, the error names both
locations, so the pieces can be put back by hand.
.SH NOTES
The command moves the repository folder, so it needs write access to the
folder that contains it. Run it outside agent sandboxes.
.PP
Folder names follow the same rule as
.BR git\-wtclone (1):
.B /
and
.B \e
in branch names become
.BR \- .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git wtmigrate ~/projects/acme/foo
Converts
.I foo
from anywhere.
.TP
.B git wtmigrate && cd ~/projects/acme/foo/main
Run inside
.IR foo ;
converts it, then moves the shell into the former main checkout (here on
branch
.IR main ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-wtclone (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1),
.BR wt (1)
